        "narration": "Marcus works at the hockey arena. Tonight the scoreboard shows the crowd size: 24 336 fans. Every digit in that number has a place, and the place tells its value.",
        "text": "24 336",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "🏒", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "Start on the left. The digit 2 is in the ten thousands place. That means 2 ten thousands, which is 20 000.",
        "text": "2 × 10 000 = 20 000",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "The 4 is in the thousands place. That is 4 thousands, or 4000. Then the 3 in the hundreds place is 3 hundreds, or 300.",
        "text": "4 × 1000 = 4000",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "The next 3 is in the tens place, so it is worth 30. The last digit, 6, is in the ones place, so it is worth 6.",
        "text": "3 × 10 = 30 and 6 × 1 = 6",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "Add the place values to get expanded form. 24 336 equals 20 000 plus 4000 plus 300 plus 30 plus 6.",
        "text": "24 336 = 20 000 + 4000 + 300 + 30 + 6",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "In words, it is twenty-four thousand three hundred thirty-six. A zero holds a place. In 40 205, there are 0 thousands and 0 tens, so those parts are left out of the expanded form.",
        "text": "40 205 = 40 000 + 200 + 5",
        "visual": null
      },
      {
        "narration": "Now you can read a number, build it, and break it apart by place value. Let's practise with some scoreboard numbers.",
        "text": null,
        "visual": null
      }
